  "text_md": "# SA SOLDIER\n\n### The official monthly magazine of the SA Department of Defence\n\n- 4\n- 5\n- 6\n\n\n## 34\n\n22\n\nFrom the Editor’s desk\n\nA visit to Air Force Base Ysterplaat Museum\n\nFuture Armour Capability Conference\n\n- 24\n- 25\n\n\nEnd of an era for the Executive National Security Programme\n\nRetire or resign with GEPF: What you need to know\n\nTraining Command bids farewell to its General Officer Commanding\n\n## 36\n\n![](<0b045ab838c05c4ff1ac844caf826f8f368d_page_2_pg1_images/imageFile1.png>)\n\nLetters to the editor\n\nGraduation ceremony of the Joint Senior Command and Staff Programme\n\n## 10\n\nSouth Africa assists Mozambique Government during the floods\n\n39\n\nChief Human Resources honours his loyal members\n\n26\n\n## 39\n\nJohannesburg Regiments Association exercises its Freedom of Entry in Soweto\n\n12 16\n\nMandela Commemoration Medal Parade\n\n28\n\n7th Warrant Officers’ Academy Certificate Ceremony\n\n40\n\nChief SANDF bestows medals for first-class service to the SANDF\n\nThe DOD participates in Chief SANDF Prestige Week\n\n29\n\nMilitary Academy awarded its students who excelled\n\n![](<0b045ab838c05c4ff1ac844caf826f8f368d_page_2_pg1_images/imageFile2.png>)\n\n42\n\nDiseases of lifestyle\n\npose a threat to the development of SA\n\n30\n\nMitchells Plain Festival\n\n43\n\n18\n\nEmbracing our colleagues with disabilities\n\n32\n\nPreparing SA youth for a nautical career\n\n18\n\nNational Civic Remembrance Sunday and Wreath-laying Ceremony\n\n#### CONTRIBUTIONS:\n\n#### REPRODUCTION, PRINTING & DISTRIBUTION:\n\nAlthough all possible care is taken with articles, the editorial staff cannot accept any responsibility for lost articles and photographs.\n\nFormeset Print (Pty) Ltd 24 Kinghall Avenue EPPINGDUST, Cape Town, 7460 Tel: (021) 507 9000 Fax: (021) 506 9092 email: formeset@formeset.co.za\n\n20\n\nSA Army observes the 96th anniversary of Armistice Day\n\nSTREET ADDRESS Defence Headquarters cor Nossob & Boeing St Erasmuskloof PRETORIA\n\n2005 - Winner of the Government Communicator of the Year Award (GCIS). 2005 - Winner of the National Ubungcweti Award (GCIS).\n\nPOSTAL ADDRESS SA SOLDIER Private Bag X158 PRETORIA, 0001\n\nTELEPHONE Tel: (012) 355 6341 Fax: (012) 355 6399 email:sasoldier@mil.za website: www.dod.mil.za\n\n#### EDITORIAL STAFF\n\nEditor: Ms Nelda Pienaar\n\nDeputy Editor: Mr Lufuno Netshirembe\n\nEditorial Staff: S Sgt Lebogang Tlhaole Sgt Itumeleng Makhubela Cpl Ally Rakoma\n\nTranslation Directorate Consultant: Language Services\n\nDistribution: Mr Jim Tshabalala\n\nTel: (012) 355 6341\n\nLayout & Design: Mr Werner van der Westhuizen\n\n2 2015 VOL 22 NO1 • S A SOL DIER\n\n",
